    "body": "In `GeneralPreferenceFragment.encryptKey`, the app derives a 128-bit value from the input key and a random salt, then returns it as hex. RVSec reports that `SecretKeyFactory.getInstance` uses `PBKDF2WithHmacSHA1`, which is not among its accepted algorithms.\n\nI use `PBKDF2WithHmacSHA256` with 100,000 iterations on API 26 and later. Older devices retain `PBKDF2WithHmacSHA1` and 65,536 iterations for platform compatibility. The salt generation, output length and hex encoding remain unchanged.\n\nI found this while running the app under RVSec, a runtime checker for how apps use the Java crypto and TLS APIs.\n\nThe project builds with this change (`assembleDebug`).\n\nI'm a Computer Engineering student at the University of Brasília (UnB), working on a research project on Android app analysis. Happy to adjust this to the project's conventions.",
